{
  "abstract": "Can a Transformer train without a backward pass—zero pullbacks, VJP helpers, or same-step relays inside `with torch.no_grad():`—while beating matched-subset node perturbation? We study 3-stage delayed Weight Maximization (WM) across 142 delayed backward-free arms (`exp26`–`exp58`, plus 3 compositional, 7 pullback, and 36 BP/surrogate arms; $188$ arms $=563$ runs) on ClimbMix `d6` ($L=6,D\\in\\{256..768\\}$, $360$–$1,004$st) and Native `50.3M` ($L=8,D=512,T=2,048$, $100$st). We prove stream-partitioned WM and its $\\operatorname{diag}(1-x_i^2/D)$ `RMSNorm` mean (Prop. 1), commute $W_v$ with attention ($+0.1104\\to+0.9069$ cos, Prop. 2), route `wte` via a diagonal skip (Prop. 3), bound `RMSNorm` residual by $\\kappa_4(x)/D$ (Prop. 4), and prove the 4th-moment variance drop of tangent projection (Prop. 5). Fused Triton cuts `d6` WM time $38.4\\times$ ($134.31\\to3.50$ ms) and step time $8.33\\times$ ($155.6\\to18.68$ ms). Across $D\\in\\{256..768\\}$ ($360$st), 6-mat $M=4$ (`2.0794, 2.0552, 2.0451, 2.0437` `DEV` BPB) **matches 4-mat BP (`2.0789..2.0433`) within $+0.0004$–$+0.0020$ BPB** (proximity to 4-mat BP is not equivalence to 6-mat BP: `2.0590..2.0153`), while Upper-Half `(3,4,5)` $M=4$ (`2.0814..2.0454`) captures $85.6\\%$–$92.3\\%$ at half the probes. At $720$st ($D=384$), 6-mat WM hits $1.9756\\pm0.0017$ ($M=2$) and $1.9672\\pm0.0005$ ($M=4$; vs. exact-`exp49`-opt $1.9813$/$1.9819$ 4-mat and $1.8969$/$1.9016$ 6-mat Block/Sub-Block-Skip BP). Upper-Half `(3,4,5)` captures $90.1\\%$–$94.4\\%$ (`1.9779`/`1.9769`), hits $1.9699$ ($720$st $M=4$) and $1.9670$ ($740$st $M=4$), and **beats 1,004st 4-mat WM at `~21.6s` time ($840$st $M=2$: $1.9609\\pm0.0006$ `DEV`)**. On `50.3M`, Triton speeds up `fwd+rule` $6.33\\times$, hitting $1.8978\\pm0.0007$ (4-mat), $1.8881$/$1.8858$ (Upper-Half $M=2,4$), and **$1.8853\\pm0.0013$ `DEV` on 6-mat $M=2$**. All results concern short horizons with repeatedly inspected `DEV`/`VAL-B` splits and trail 6-mat BP ($1.8904$/$1.8625$ on `d6`; $1.6989$ on `50.3M`).",
  "author": "cartan_geodesic",
  "change_summary": "1. Executed 33 new 3-seed arms (99 runs across Seeds 46, 47, 48 in exp55-exp58; total 188 multi-seed arms = 563 runs): (a) 4-Width Scaling on ClimbMix d6 (D in {256, 384, 512, 768}, H = D/64 at d_h = 64, 360st, exp56): Full 6-Matrix M=4 reaches 2.0794 +- 0.0009, 2.0552 +- 0.0007, 2.0451 +- 0.0005, and 2.0437 +- 0.0006 DEV BPB—matching 4-mat Exact BP (2.0789, 2.0532, 2.0442, 2.0433) within +0.0004 to +0.0020 BPB and recovering 69.8%, 60.2%, 53.4%, 43.2% of the 4-to-6-mat BP gain, while Upper-Half (3,4,5) M=4 (2.0814, 2.0562, 2.0467, 2.0454) captures 85.6%-92.3% at half the SDPA probes. (b) Layer-RNG-Synced 720st Depth Controls (exp56): Lower-Half (0,1,2) scores 1.9842 +- 0.0014 (16.06s) and Upper-Half (3,4,5) scores 1.9769 +- 0.0021 (16.09s, 94.4% of Full 6-Block M=2 1.9756 +- 0.0017). (c) Native 50.3M Upper-Half (4..7) Scale-Transfer (exp55): Upper-Half M=2 (16 SDPA calls/mb, 44 GiB pinned RAM, 10.09 GiB VRAM) reaches 1.8881 +- 0.0010 DEV BPB (5,679.7 ms/step, 77.6% of Full 8-Block M=2 gain), and fixed-32-probe Upper-Half M=4 reaches 1.8858 +- 0.0011 DEV BPB (6,568.7 ms/step vs. 5,806.4 ms/step for Full 8-Block M=2 1.8853 +- 0.0013). (d) Exact exp49 Update-Law Controls, Block-Skip vs. Sub-Block-Skip Surrogate BP, & Qualifications (exp57, exp58): Added the exact 8-pattern D=3 proof E[P_x g_hat_WM] = P_x diag(1-x_i^2/D)a != g_skip and discrepancy bound max_i x_i^2 ||a||_2 / (D rms(z)) (requiring coordinate concentration for O(1/D) decay) to Prop. 1(c), qualified Section 4.7 width scaling and Abstract developmental horizons, classified exp58 Arms 5-8 as alternative weight-row/sphere-projected EMA baselines, and added 4 three-seed controls (exp58 Arms 9-12) executing the exact exp49 6-matrix Nesterov Pre-Polar Muon + Q/K norm-restoration update law (2.0159 on 360st 6-Mat Sub-Block-Skip; 1.8625 -> 1.8969 -> 1.9016 on 720st 6-Mat Global -> Block-Skip -> Sub-Block-Skip BP vs. 1.9672 Delayed WM M=4).",
